<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uyghur Muqam</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> Muqam is the classical music tradition of the Uyghurs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a>, a set of large suites combining songs, dances, poetry and instrumental music. Tradition credits the compilation of the Twelve Muqam to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amannisa-khan">Amannisa Khan</a> at the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yarkent-khanate">Yarkent Khanate</a> in the 16th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a> recognises it as part of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity.</p></div>
